    overview: "This commercial warehouse in Toano, in James City County, is owned by a real estate services company. It is a multi-gable metal building of about 18,000 square feet, with several roof sections meeting in long valleys.\n\nThe owner wants to lease space in the building. The roof had a lot of damaged metal panels, and the building had no insulation at all, which makes it hard to rent. The owner needed a roof that would stop the damage problem and make the space more usable for a tenant.",
    challenge: "Replacing the damaged panels across a building this size would have been a big job and a big expense. Our before photos show worn, stained metal across the gables and long valleys where the roof sections meet, which are areas that collect water and debris.\n\nThe lack of insulation was the other half of the problem. An uninsulated metal building gets very hot in summer and cold in winter, and adding insulation from the inside of an occupied or leasable warehouse brings its own cost and disruption.",
    solution: "We cleaned the roof and installed a spray foam roof system over the existing metal, then coated it. Spraying the foam on the outside let us avoid replacing the damaged panels, and the foam added R-10 insulation to the roof.",
