    whyThisSystem: "Spray foam fixed both problems with one system. Because it bonds directly to the metal and forms a continuous layer, it covers damaged panels, seams and fasteners without removing them. Because it is also insulation, putting it on the outside of the roof insulates the building without any interior work. Foam needs a coating over it for UV protection, and a light-colored coating also reflects sunlight, which helps a metal building stay cooler.",
