    challenge: "On an EPDM roof, the seams are usually the weak point. The sheets are joined with adhesive or seam tape, and over the years those seams can open or lift. Seam lines ran across the black membrane at regular intervals.\n\nBlack EPDM also absorbs a lot of heat in the Virginia Beach sun. The roof had to be cleaned well before any restoration product would bond to it.",
    solution: "We cleaned the EPDM membrane, applied reinforced sealant on every seam, and then coated the roof. Every seam was reinforced, leaving white stripes across the black membrane, before the full coating went on.",
    steps: ["We cleaned the full EPDM membrane to prepare it for the restoration products.", "We prepared each seam along its full length.", "We applied reinforced sealant over every seam.", "We coated the full roof surface."],
    whyThisSystem: "If an EPDM membrane is still in reasonable shape, restoring it costs far less than tearing it off and replacing it. Since the seams are where EPDM roofs usually fail, reinforcing every seam addresses the main weak point directly. The coating then covers the whole membrane and protects it from the sun. A white coating over black rubber also reflects much more sunlight, so the roof surface runs cooler.",
    results: ["Full cleaning of the EPDM membrane", "Reinforced sealant on every seam", "Finished coating over the whole roof", "White roof surface in place of black rubber"],
    faqs: [
      { question: "Can an EPDM rubber roof be coated?", answer: "Yes. EPDM can be restored with a coating made to bond to rubber, as long as the membrane is cleaned thoroughly and primed where the manufacturer calls for it. Seams and penetrations are reinforced first, then the coating is applied across the roof." },
      { question: "Why do EPDM roofs leak at the seams?", answer: "EPDM sheets are joined with adhesive or seam tape. Over time, heat, cold and movement can weaken those bonds and let the seams lift or open. That is why seam reinforcement is the first step in most EPDM restorations." },
    ],
