    whyThisSystem: "A targeted repair made sense here because the problem was local, not roof-wide. Covering a whole roof to chase one leak is expensive, and if the source is never found, a new layer can hide it without fixing it. The better approach is to find where water is actually getting in, fix that detail properly, and protect the area so it stays sealed. On metal roofs, that usually means looking hard at seams, fasteners, laps and transitions, where water can get in and run a long way before it shows.",
